    "question": {
      ":question/id": "898c157a-e60f-5225-a854-9623ec4d2dfe",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\cos\\left(t+\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)$ in terms of $\\sin t$ or $\\cos t$.\n\nUse the formula\n\n$$\n\\cos(u+v)=\\cos u\\cos v-\\sin u\\sin v\n$$\n\nand the exact values $\\cos\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)=0$ and $\\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)=-1$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u+v)=\\cos u\\cos v-\\sin u\\sin v\n$$\n\nWith $u=t$ and $v=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$, the exact values are $\\cos\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)=0$ and $\\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)=-1$. Substitute and collect the terms in the requested order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos\\left(t+\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)&=\\cos t\\cos\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)-\\sin t\\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\cos t\\cdot\\left(0\\right)-\\sin t\\cdot\\left(-1\\right)\\\\\n&=\\sin t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
